    "summary": "A weaving-sample; a length of weft ikat, &#039;matmi&#039;, patterned shot silk; tabby woven.  Two main registers: two lines of pink/white confronted nagas (snakes), the ends of their bodies touching; patterning in lower register slightly longer and wider than upper.  A white fuzzy line separates this imagery from a geometric band below; a diamond-within-diamond pattern.  Brown warp, red weft; cloth for a tube skirt, a &#039;phasin&#039;?; patterning worn as bands.  Chemically dyed yarns.  Warp ends raw.  Unused.",
